{"700":{"assignees":[],"author":"qingkwl","base":"main","body":"## Summary\n\nAdds the JiuwenSwarm startup-latency work as **one consolidated patch** (`0010-jw-startup-latency.patch`, ~35s of per-launch savings). The changes were developed and measured on the Windows desktop line (same-machine A/B against gateway startup stage logs):\n\n| change | measured saving |\n|---|---|\n| feishu SDK lazy import (it was imported even with the channel disabled) | ~4.7s |\n| `tui_connect` preload off the critical path | ~1.8s |\n| channel-config settle window 0.75s -> 0.2s | ~0.55s |\n| heartbeat import chain deferred | ~2.8s |\n| AgentServer import slimming (pandas/pdfplumber/milvus out of the import path) | ~6.8s |\n| Gateway<->AgentServer connect unblocked from warmup | ~9.5s |\n| post-listen warmups gated behind the first request | ~15.6s |\n\nEnd-to-end on the Windows desktop: warm restart ~17.5s -> ~5-7s; user-perceived cold start 50s+ -> 20-25s.\n\n**Why one patch instead of seven**: the changes overlap on `app_gateway.py` / `agent_ws_server.py`, and a chain where several patches edit the same region cannot pass the idempotent-reapply contract (`swarm-patches.py apply` twice must be a no-op — the `--reverse --check` skip needs each patch's post-state intact). Consolidating keeps one patch per file region, matching the upstream patch-set convention.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `swarm-patches.py apply` on a clean `workswarm0.2.6` checkout with 0001-0009 + this patch — passes\n- [x] **second `apply` over the already-patched tree — no-op (the previously failing idempotency case)**\n- [x] `swarm-patches.py verify` — passes\n- [ ] CI green\n","ci":{"checks":[{"conclusion":"success","name":"Select CI policy","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/41018155789/job/123939081027"},{"conclusion":"success","name":"L1 (static checks)","url":"https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/actions/runs/41018155789/job/123939150845"},{"conclusion":"skipped",